-- ADR-007 migration: version 1 -> version 2.
--
-- Adds the per-waypoint sharing policy required by master blueprint Phase 10 §10.6
-- ("Sharing is explicit and controllable"). Without a field the policy cannot be
-- expressed, and the operator cannot tell which of their existing waypoints may be
-- shared.
--
-- DEFAULT IS THE MOST RESTRICTIVE VALUE, and that is a deliberate product decision
-- rather than a convenience. §10.6 requires EXPLICIT OPT-IN, so a waypoint that
-- existed before this column must NOT become shared merely because the app was
-- upgraded. Defaulting to anything more permissive would silently publish a user's
-- existing field data to peers they never chose to share it with, and the user
-- would have no way to learn that had happened.
--
-- A user who wants a waypoint shared must open it and change the policy. That is
-- one extra action per waypoint, and it is the whole point.
--
-- ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN preserves every existing row, which the destructive
-- alternative (drop and recreate) would not. This database holds waypoints, track
-- points, and offline pack records on hardware that may be offline and unable to
-- restore a backup.

ALTER TABLE Waypoint ADD COLUMN sharingPolicy TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PRIVATE';
